  "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n\nLet $Y=2{X}^{2}-2.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $b$ | $6$ | $16$ | $30$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $c$ | $d$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $c-a?$",
